<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Govinda Vidyadhara</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. <a href="/years/1541">1541</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Govinda Vidyadhara was a minister of the Gajapati Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Odisha</a> who in 1541 killed the last heirs of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prataparudra-deva">Prataparudra Deva</a> and seized the throne at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuttack">Cuttack</a>. He founded the short-lived Bhoi dynasty, which inherited a kingdom already reduced by Vijayanagara and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golconda-fort">Golconda</a> and fell to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karrani-dynasty">Karrani Afghans</a> in 1568.</p></div>
